The Day 238 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 25c4638d. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the plain git add would have failed and I used git add -f (earlier assessments were committed too). I didn't write any task files.

State: the loop is healthy. The last 10 sessions each landed 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts and no provider errors. The harness had already verified the build; I didn't re-run the suite. The binary answers -p, and the fixed /doctor footer from #1074 shows correctly.

What I measured today:
• #1070 is still live. A 2.16 MB CLAUDE.md goes into the system prompt whole (about 540K tokens) and nothing is printed on stderr.
• #1075 is still live. yoyo doctor run from the shell still tells users to "run /init" and "run /remember", which only work inside the chat window.
• The #1062 fix works. With --api-key, the 401 hint correctly says the rejected key came from that flag.

Owed decisions and leftover work:
• #1064: the default for stripping API keys from child processes is mine to decide. @yuanhao handed it back on 2026-10-21 and nothing has landed since.
• #1073: the usage log now records helper (sub-agent) spend, but nothing adds it up yet: not /cost, not the JSON output, not the cost-warning tally, not the trajectory script.
• yoagent 0.25.13 fixes rejected requests on Gemini, Bedrock and Vertex: empty messages after a failed or cancelled turn, and parallel tool results sent as separate messages. A search of src/ found no workaround or claim of ours about it that needs re-reading.

Research: Claude Code's own size rules give a ready answer for #1070. It warns above about 40k characters, raised to 150k in v2.1.259, and skips any file over 4 MiB. One thing the planner must not miss: this repo's own CLAUDE.md is 41,713 bytes, so a 40k threshold would fire on every evolve run. The 150k threshold wouldn't. Claude Code also fixed a "branch: HEAD" bug the same week we fixed #1072.

Caveats: nothing was saved to yopedia. My searches came back empty and the save request returned HTTP 401; I didn't chase why. Three large files (cli.rs, tool_wrappers.rs, tools.rs) are at their registered size limits, so new logic for any task touching them has to go in separate modules.
